        "authoredOn": "2026-06-07T08:12:00Z",
        "reasonCode": [{"text": "Sore throat and nasal congestion"}],
        "note": [
          {"text": "HPI: 34-year-old woman with two days of sore throat and nasal congestion, mild (3/10), no fever, breathing or swallowing difficulty. No significant medical history. Picture is consistent with a self-limiting upper respiratory tract infection."},
          {"text": "Action: Rest and maintain fluid intake."},
          {"text": "Action: Paracetamol or ibuprofen as needed for discomfort."},
          {"text": "Action: Seek care if symptoms persist beyond 10 days, or if breathing difficulty, high fever, or neck swelling develop."},
          {"text": "Guideline: 0.79|Self-limiting URTI management (NICE NG79 summary)|Most upper respiratory tract infections are self-limiting and resolve within 1-2 weeks with supportive care; antibiotics are not routinely indicated in the absence of red-flag features."},
          {"text": "QR: demo-case2-qr"}
        ]
      }
