        "authoredOn": "2026-06-07T09:05:00Z",
        "reasonCode": [{"text": "Sudden severe breathlessness and wheeze"}],
        "note": [
          {"text": "HPI: 44-year-old woman with asthma presenting with sudden, rapidly worsening breathlessness and wheeze over one hour, severe (9/10), with chest tightness and poor response to repeated reliever inhaler use. Oxygen saturation 91%. Features are consistent with an acute severe asthma exacerbation requiring emergency assessment."},
          {"text": "Action: Call emergency services now; do not drive yourself."},
          {"text": "Action: Keep using the reliever inhaler (with a spacer if available) while waiting for help."},
          {"text": "Action: Sit upright and stay as calm as possible."},
          {"text": "Red flag: poor response to reliever inhaler"},
          {"text": "Red flag: oxygen saturation below 92%"},
          {"text": "Guideline: 0.91|Acute asthma severity assessment (BTS/SIGN summary)|Acute severe asthma is indicated by inability to complete sentences, respiratory rate or pulse elevation, or peak flow 33-50% of best; oxygen saturation below 92% suggests a life-threatening attack requiring immediate emergency treatment."},
